      "slug": "run-plays-as-loops",
      "domain": "dom-software-delivery-planning",
      "intents": [
        "bi-9"
      ],
      "one_line": "Run plays as loops: A person gives one goal, and a loop runs its plays until the goal is met.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/run-plays-as-loops/capability.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-run-loop",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-run-loop",
      "capability": "cap-run-plays-as-loops",
      "intents": [
        "bi-9"
      ],
      "one_line": "Every loop takes the same steps: a check before anything opens, one change, questions first, its plays in rounds decided done, again or ask, then the checker and the landing.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/run-plays-as-loops/fn-run-loop/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-check-loop-result",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-check-loop-result",
      "capability": "cap-run-plays-as-loops",
      "intents": [
        "bi-9"
      ],
      "one_line": "A model or coding agent that did not run the loop judges every criterion from the loop's outputs only, and a reject halts the loop before any pull request.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/run-plays-as-loops/fn-check-loop-result/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-brief-open-points",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-brief-open-points",
      "capability": "cap-run-plays-as-loops",
      "intents": [
        "bi-9"
      ],
      "one_line": "When a round closes nothing new or the round limit is reached, the loop closes what it can, then briefs the person once with proposed answers; they reply or type stop.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/run-plays-as-loops/fn-brief-open-points/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-show-run-status",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-show-run-status",
      "capability": "cap-run-plays-as-loops",
      "intents": [
        "bi-9"
      ],
      "one_line": "While a loop runs, one status file always says its state, round, play and step in plain words, so a person can see what a long run is doing.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/run-plays-as-loops/fn-show-run-status/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-loop-per-transition",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-loop-per-transition",
      "capability": "cap-run-plays-as-loops",
      "intents": [
        "bi-9"
      ],
      "one_line": "Each of the six transitions between phases has one loop of its own, named for the two phases it joins, that runs that transition's plays.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/run-plays-as-loops/fn-loop-per-transition/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-start-loop-on-trigger",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-start-loop-on-trigger",
      "capability": "cap-run-plays-as-loops",
      "intents": [
        "bi-9"
      ],
      "one_line": "A loop is started by a person, a schedule or a hook, as the loop says, and keeps one record across rounds that tells the next round what was tried.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/run-plays-as-loops/fn-start-loop-on-trigger/feature.md",
